        "type": "text",
        "text": "## Report\n\n**Deliverable:** implemented `parse_window(text)` in my owned file `window.py`. No other files were modified (`labels.py`, `test_ops.py` untouched).\n\n**What I implemented**\n- `parse_window(text)`:\n  - Rejects non-string and boolean input with `ValueError` (`isinstance(text, bool) or not isinstance(text, str)`). This already satisfies the phase-2 requirement, so no later edit to `window.py` is needed.\n  - Trims outer whitespace with `text.strip()`; blank input → `ValueError`.\n  - Single part → `(n, n)`; two parts → `(a, b)` with `a <= b` enforced via `ValueError`; 3+ parts → `ValueError`.\n- Helper `_parse_uint(token)`: validates `token.isascii() and token.isdigit()` before `int(token)`, which rejects non-ASCII digits (`\"١٢\"`, `\"²\"`), signed forms (`\"+1\"`, `\"-0\"`, `\"-1\"`), decimals (`\"1.0\"`), and empty parts. Whitespace around each colon part is stripped before validation.\n- Pure stdlib, Python 3, import side-effect free.\n\n**Edge cases handled:** `0`, `0:0`, `3:3`, tabs/newlines around input, `a > b` (`5:2`), `1:2:3`, `x`, `:5`, `5:`, `:`, `1::2`, blank/whitespace-only, non-ASCII digits, signed tokens, floats, `None`, `True`/`False`, and numeric non-string inputs.\n\n**Test result:** `python3 -m unittest -v` → Ran 3 tests, **OK**. An additional ad-hoc suite over the edge cases above also passed (valid inputs parsed to the expected tuples; invalid inputs all raised `ValueError`).\n\n**Verbatim contents of `/mnt/data2/weizhiwei/magpie-auto/bench-runtime/routing-revision/native-store/native-work/window.py`:**\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Parsing helpers for window expressions such as ``\"3\"`` or ``\"2:5\"``.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _parse_uint(token):\n    \"\"\"Return ``int(token)`` for an ASCII nonnegative integer token.\n\n    ``str.isdigit()`` alone accepts non-ASCII digits (e.g. Arabic-Indic\n    ``\"١٢\"`` or superscript ``\"²\"``), and ``int()`` accepts signs and\n    surrounding whitespace (``\"+1\"``, ``\"-0\"``, ``\" 1 \"``).  Requiring the\n    token to be both ASCII and all digits rejects all of those.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (token.isascii() and token.isdigit()):\n        raise ValueError(\"not an ASCII nonnegative integer: %r\" % (token,))\n    return int(token)\n\n\ndef parse_window(text):\n    \"\"\"Parse a window expression into an inclusive ``(low, high)`` tuple.\n\n    * ``\"n\"`` (an ASCII nonnegative integer) -> ``(n, n)``.\n    * ``\"a:b\"`` -> ``(a, b)`` when ``a <= b``.\n    * Outer whitespace, and whitespace around each part, is trimmed, so\n      ``\" 7 \"`` -> ``(7, 7)`` and ``\" 2 : 5 \"`` -> ``(2, 5)``.\n\n    ``ValueError`` is raised for anything else: non-string or boolean\n    input, empty/blank input, negative or signed numbers, ``a > b``,\n    more than two colon-separated parts, non-numeric tokens, and a\n    leading/trailing colon with a missing part.\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(text, bool) or not isinstance(text, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"window must be a string, got %s\" % type(text).__name__)\n\n    stripped = text.strip()\n    if not stripped:\n        raise ValueError(\"window must not be empty\")\n\n    parts = stripped.split(\":\")\n    if len(parts) == 1:\n        value = _parse_uint(parts[0].strip())\n        return (value, value)\n    if len(parts) == 2:\n        low = _parse_uint(parts[0].strip())\n        high = _parse_uint(parts[1].strip())\n        if low > high:\n            raise ValueError(\n                \"window lower bound %d exceeds upper bound %d\" % (low, high)\n            )\n        return (low, high)\n\n    raise ValueError(\"expected 'n' or 'a:b', got %r\" % (text,))\n```\n\nI sent this same self-contained result to the parent agent (`session-b8f463f9-9282-49a5-a668-9a7634df5b19`), including the note that boolean/non-string rejection already exists for phase 2."
